# OBSERVABILITY

Production failures must be visible, attributable, and actionable — without leaking PII or secrets.

## Stack

| Capability | Source of truth |
|---|---|
| Crash reporting | Sentry client (`src/lib/sentry.js`) + API (`api/instrument.mjs`) |
| Performance | Browser tracing + web vitals (Sentry); API traces; optional profiling |
| Structured logging | `api/_lib/safeLog.js` JSON levels + `requestId`; client `reportError` |
| Health checks | `GET /api/functions/health` (+ `?deep=1` with ops secret) |
| Analytics | First-party allowlisted events (`productAnalytics.js`); opt-out in Privacy |
| Audit trails | `audit_events` + `writeAuditEvent` (admin/money mutations) |
| Feature flags | `featureFlags.js` defaults + `/api/functions/featureFlags` |
| Session replay | Sentry Replay — masked, opt-in (`session_replay` + `VITE_SENTRY_REPLAY`) |
| Alerting | `OPS_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL` / Slack on 5xx + money-path captures |

## Privacy rules

- `sendDefaultPii: false`; opaque user id only
- Replay: mask all text/inputs; block media; off until user opts in
- Analytics: allowlisted event names; no emails, tokens, GPS coordinates, or free-text bodies
- Logs: redact secrets via `safeLog.redactValue`
- Audit metadata: no secrets; hash IPs when recorded

## Definition of done

Incomplete if money/auth failures are silent, if new admin mutations skip audit, if replay runs without consent, or if health/readiness no longer reflects money-path readiness.
